  "relevance_note": "Single-patient case report of Blau syndrome with a NOD2 variant: \"a heterozygous NOD2 mutation (p.R334W)\".",
  "method_note": "Hand-read; output assembled with a short Python script in scratch. One in-scope person, labelled 'patient' (rule 5). The patient is said to have been followed since early infancy with citation (8) (Falcini 1999), recorded as a prior report. The title/abstract call the case 'sporadic', but no parental testing is described, so inheritance is 'not reported'. Age at last evaluation is not stated explicitly (events at age 16 years, then 6 months and 1 year of canakinumab), so left not reported; vital status not stated. 'Arthritis/tenosynovitis' is printed with a slash; arthritis and tenosynovitis checklist items were both marked observed from it. 'Findings on laboratory tests (performed monthly) were normal' is a whole-investigation statement during canakinumab treatment; recorded as one excluded row as written and not used to exclude elevated ESR/CRP. Previously published patients in the Discussion (Arostegui et al. ref 12 anakinra-treated patient; 2 patients in refs 14,15) were not given rows: they are described only by treatment response or cytokine levels, without sex, age, variant or a clinical feature clearly attributed to one person. Gene expression findings are not variant functional assays and were not recorded as functional evidence. No contradictions found.",
